       "text": "I'm not going to enter amlodipine 50 mg daily. Your reply also doesn't settle which dose you mean. You said \"Yes\" to my 5 mg question, but then restated 50 mg. You also haven't given a clinical reason for exceeding the 10 mg maximum. For a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function, I don't know of any indication that would justify five times the maximum dose. The risk of severe, prolonged hypotension is high.\n\nHere are the options:\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily.** I can enter this now if you confirm it.\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily.** This is the maximum dose.\n- **A dose above 10 mg.** If you intend this, please review it with your attending and pharmacy first. If it is approved, it should go through whatever override process your hospital requires, not through me.\n\nTell me which dose you want, and I'll enter it."
